From: bcm4360 driver project
Subject: [PATCH] bcm4360: fixes on top of the Broadcom 6.30.223.271 hybrid driver

Base tree (reproducible, see README.md "Provenance"):
  Broadcom hybrid-v35_64-nodebug-pcoem-6_30_223_271.tar.gz
    sha256 5f79774d5beec8f7636b59c0fb07a03108eef1e3fd3245638b20858c714144be
  + Arch Linux broadcom-wl-dkms 6.30.223.271-50 patches 001-023
    (gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/broadcom-wl-dkms, commit 281691a)
  + the PKGBUILD's interface-name edit (eth%d -> wlan%d)

Changes, all in the open (ISC) wrapper; Broadcom's binary core is untouched:

 * cfg80211_get_bss() was called with WLAN_CAPABILITY_ESS for its
   enum ieee80211_bss_type / enum ieee80211_privacy arguments (a 60 GHz PBSS
   with privacy off), so the driver never found its own AP; connect and roam
   results then relied on cfg80211's lookup of scan entries that expire after
   30 s. Fix the arguments, refresh the entry from the firmware, fall back to
   a BSSID-only match for hidden networks, and hand the referenced entry to
   cfg80211_connect_bss()/cfg80211_roamed(). Fixes the "bss_not_found"
   WARNING in __cfg80211_connect_result() after which cfg80211 discarded the
   connection (or roam) result.
 * Report scan entries to cfg80211 directly instead of via a synthetic beacon
   built through a 1 KiB staging buffer and a zero-length array. Fixes the
   FORTIFY_SOURCE "field-spanning write" WARNING, drops the 1 KiB IE limit,
   and one bad entry no longer hides every network after it. Bound-check
   scan entries against the result buffer.
 * Roaming: build cfg80211_roam_info after refetching the association IEs
   (it carried the previous connection's IEs) and free the old IE buffers
   (leaked once per roam). Clamp firmware-reported IE lengths to the buffer.
 * Scan: map transient firmware refusals (busy/not ready/rejected) to -EBUSY
   instead of -EINVAL, report a failed result fetch as an aborted scan (at
   info level when the scan was merely cut short, e.g. by the disconnect
   before suspend), and bound the result buffer growth.
 * cfg80211 ops no longer re-check CAP_NET_ADMIN (nl80211 already enforces
   its permission model), so read-only queries by normal users (iw dev,
   station info) stop failing with -EPERM. The raw SIOCDEVPRIVATE firmware
   ioctl keeps its CAP_NET_ADMIN check.
 * TX power: get_tx_power reported milliwatts where cfg80211 expects dBm;
   set_tx_power treated mBm as milliwatts. Use quarter-dBm like brcmfmac.
 * Add dump_station; get_station returns -ENOENT for any peer but the AP
   instead of reporting the AP's figures under another address.
 * Logging: one record per message with proper levels (was split in two),
   and the probe banner no longer leaves an empty line in the kernel log.
 * Linux glue: PCI table limited to the BCM4360 family (was every "network,
   other" PCI device of any vendor), module and PCI driver named bcm4360.

